From d51c64eb33a8c40a97efd6938c323c2b293b256c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CustomKIMI <customkimi@localhost>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:45:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 05/13] customkimi: show the active provider's balance in the
 web UI

kimi web and /web show a small badge before the composer's model picker with the balance of the provider serving the open session's model (ClosedRouter or 7api). If a web UI update moves the picker, the badge falls back to a corner pill. kap-server gets two generic hooks: startServer({ extraRoutes, webHtmlInjection }) and an htmlInjection option on the web asset routes. The CLI registers GET /customkimi/balance-badge.js and GET /api/customkimi/balance?model=<alias> (bearer auth like every /api route), answered by the same BillingMonitor as the TUI footer. The browser script reads the web UI's stored credential and the open session's model from the public session API, and never retries a rejected credential, so it cannot trip the failed-auth rate limit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
